# Runtime data directories, anchored to the repo root with a leading slash.
#
# Anchoring is not cosmetic here. A bare `models/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, and it silently excluded backend/app/db/models — the entire
# SQLAlchemy models package — from the first commit. Nothing complained locally,
# because the files were still on disk; CI checked out a tree where env.py could
# not import them. Keep the leading slash on anything named after a concept that
# could also be a source package.
/data/
/models/
/backups/
/audio_cache/
*.db
*.sqlite3

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local model weights — gigabytes, and re-downloadable. Unanchored on purpose:
# weights are unwelcome wherever they appear.
*.gguf
